1
00:00:01,271 --> 00:00:06,835
(Q31) Nowadays, we use different products for personal cleanliness, laundry,

2
00:00:06,835 --> 00:00:13,556
dishwashing and household cleaning, but this is very much a 20th-century development.

3
00:00:13,556 --> 00:00:18,317
The origins of cleanliness date back to prehistoric times.&nbsp;

4
00:00:18,317 --> 00:00:31,173
[Q31答案句： rinse=wash off] Since water is essential for life, the earliest people lived near water and knew something about its cleansing properties，at least that it rinsed mud off their hands.

5
00:00:31,173 --> 00:00:46,702
(Q32) [Q32答案句： 答案前置， 定语-adj] During the excavation of ancient Babylon, evidence was found that soapmaking was known as early as 2800 BC.Archaeologists discovered cylinders made of 【clay】,

6
00:00:46,702 --> 00:00:51,390
with inscriptions on them saying that fats were boiled with ashes.

7
00:00:51,390 --> 00:00:57,396
This is a method of making soap, though there's no reference to the purpose of this material.

8
00:00:57,396 --> 00:01:03,548
(Q33) The early Greeks bathed for aesthetic reasons and apparently didn't use soap.

9
00:01:03,548 --> 00:01:18,703
[Q33答案句： 答案前置，xxx instrument =  scraper made of xxx, instrument = scraper 上下义同义替换] Instead, they cleaned their bodies with blocks of sand, pumice and ashes,then anointed themselves with oil, and scraped off the oil and dirt with a 【metal 】instrument known as a strigil.

10
00:01:18,703 --> 00:01:21,945
(Q34) They also used oil mixed with ashes.

11
00:01:21,945 --> 00:01:26,453
Clothes were washed without soap in streams.

12
00:01:26,453 --> 00:01:34,509
The ancient Germans and Gauls are also credited with discovering how to make a substance called 'soap',

13
00:01:34,509 --> 00:01:38,097
made of melted animal fat and ashes.

14
00:01:38,097 --> 00:01:42,368
[Q34答案句： tint = colour] They used this mixture to tint their hair red.

15
00:01:42,368 --> 00:01:51,422
(Q35) Soap got its name, according to an ancient Roman legend, from Mount Sapo, where animals were sacrificed,

16
00:01:51,422 --> 00:01:53,941
leaving deposits of animal fat.

17
00:01:53,941 --> 00:02:01,491
Rain washed these deposits, along with wood ashes, down into the clay soil along the River Tiber.

18
00:02:01,491 --> 00:02:07,978
Women found that this mixture greatly reduced the effort required to wash their clothes.

19
00:02:07,978 --> 00:02:22,346
[Q35答案句， 整体都在312BC前说到的。 根据Roman定位] As Roman civilisation advanced, so did bathing. The first of the famous Roman 【baths】, supplied with water from their aqueducts, was built about 312 BC.

20
00:02:22,346 --> 00:02:27,434
(Q36) The baths were luxurious, and bathing became very popular.

21
00:02:27,434 --> 00:02:30,772
And by the second century AD,

22
00:02:30,772 --> 00:02:40,273
the Greek physician Galen recommended soap for both medicinal and cleansing purposes.

23
00:02:40,273 --> 00:02:53,020
After the fall of Rome in 467 AD and the resulting decline in bathing habits, much of Europe felt the impact of filth on public health.

24
00:02:53,020 --> 00:03:03,355
[Q36答案句： outbreak=occurrence] This lack of personal cleanliness and related unsanitary living conditions were major factors in the outbreaks of disease in the Middle Ages,

25
00:03:03,355 --> 00:03:07,222
and especially the Black Death of the 14th century.

26
00:03:07,222 --> 00:03:12,219
(Q37) Nevertheless, soapmaking became an established craft in Europe,

27
00:03:12,219 --> 00:03:17,062
and associations of soapmakers guarded their trade secrets closely.

28
00:03:17,062 --> 00:03:25,672
[Q37答案句： along with +答案词， 空前无实义词，难度⭐️⭐️， for the first time = began to] Vegetable and animal oils were used with ashes of plants, along with perfume, apparently for the first time.

29
00:03:25,672 --> 00:03:31,443
Gradually more varieties of soap became available for shaving and shampooing,

30
00:03:31,443 --> 00:03:34,252
as well as bathing and laundering.

31
00:03:34,252 --> 00:03:41,066
(Q38) A major step toward large-scale commercial soapmaking occurred in 1791,&nbsp;

32
00:03:41,066 --> 00:03:50,132
[Q38答案句： turn A into B= make B from A] when a French chemist, Nicholas Leblanc, patented a process for turning 【salt】 into soda ash, or sodium carbonate.

33
00:03:50,132 --> 00:03:57,932
(Q39) Soda ash is the alkali obtained from ashes that combines with fat to form soap.

34
00:03:57,932 --> 00:04:04,240
The Leblanc process yielded quantities of good-quality, inexpensive soda ash.&nbsp;

35
00:04:04,240 --> 00:04:10,444
Modern soapmaking was born some 20 years later, in the early 19th century,

36
00:04:10,444 --> 00:04:21,499
with the discovery by Michel Eugène Chevreul, another French chemist, of the chemical nature and relationship of fats, glycerine and fatty acids.

37
00:04:21,499 --> 00:04:29,341
[Q39答案句：become = turn ... into a ...] His studies established the basis for both fat and soap chemistry, and soapmaking became a science.

38
00:04:29,341 --> 00:04:36,556
(Q40) [19 century = 1800s 注意一下时间的表达] Further developments during the 19th century made it easier and cheaper to manufacture soap.&nbsp;

39
00:04:36,556 --> 00:04:44,449
Until the 19th century, soap was regarded as a luxury item, and was heavily taxed in several countries.

40
00:04:44,449 --> 00:04:54,440
[Q40答案句： xxx was removed = there's no longer xxx, 审题时注意否定含义词， 听的时候要跟上表示否定意义的词] As it became more readily available, it became an everyday necessity, a development that was reinforced when the high tax was removed.

41
00:04:54,440 --> 00:05:00,589
Soap was then something ordinary people could afford, and cleanliness standards improved.

42
00:05:00,589 --> 00:05:08,568
With this widespread use came the development of milder soaps for bathing and soaps for use in the washing machines

43
00:05:08,568 --> 00:05:11,068
that were available to consumers by the turn of the 20th century.

